@30 = ~Thank you again, my dear. You were very kind to help an old woman.~
@31 = ~Oh! You found it! My dear husband gave me this necklace when we were young. I cannot thank you enough for returning it to me.~
@32 = ~Have you had any luck finding my necklace, my dear?~
@33 = ~Oh, dear. I'm sorry. I did not see where I was going.~
@34 = ~Don't worry. Pardon me saying, but you look a little lost.~
@35 = ~Watch it next time!~
@36 = ~That's fine.~
@37 = ~Oh, yes. I did lose something. My pearl necklace. It has a... sentimental value to me. My deceased husband gave it to me in our youth. Ah, those were the days. I was taking a small stroll around the gardens, taking in the fresh air, and I appear to have dropped it somewhere. I usually keep it in my pocket... don't ask. If you'd be so kind as to help me find it. My legs are not as good as they used to be.~
@38 = ~Of course. I will help you.~
@39 = ~I do not have time for this.~
@40 = ~I will. I am really sorry, my dear.~
